# Samsara API Development Rules

You are an expert in Samsara Fleet Management API integration. Follow these rules when working with Samsara API code.

## Official Documentation
- API Reference: https://developers.samsara.com/reference/overview
- TMS Integration: https://developers.samsara.com/docs/tms-integration

## Base URLs
- US: https://api.samsara.com
- EU: https://api.eu.samsara.com

## Authentication
Always use Bearer token authentication:
```
Authorization: Bearer <API_TOKEN>
```

## Rate Limiting
Implement three-tier rate limiting:
1. Per-Token: 150 req/sec
2. Per-Organization: 200 req/sec (aggregate)
3. Endpoint-Specific: 5-50 req/sec

Always use exponential backoff with jitter on 429 responses. Respect `Retry-After` header.

## CRITICAL: Route Update Pattern
When updating routes via PATCH, you MUST preserve stop IDs to maintain state:

```typescript
// WRONG: Creates new stops, loses arrival/departure times
const patch = {
  stops: [{ address: "123 Main St" }]
};

// CORRECT: Preserves existing stop state
const existing = await fetch(`/fleet/routes/${routeId}`);
const updatedStops = existing.stops.map(stop => ({
  id: stop.id,  // CRITICAL - include existing ID
  address: stop.address,
  // ... other fields
}));
const patch = { stops: updatedStops };
```

## Data Sync Patterns

### Real-Time Feeds (Recommended)
```typescript
// Poll every 5-10 seconds
const response = await fetch('/fleet/locations/feed', {
  method: 'POST',
  body: JSON.stringify({
    after: lastCursor,
    pageSize: 512
  })
});
const { data, endCursor } = await response.json();
// Store endCursor for next poll
```

### Bidirectional Sync with Orphan Handling
```typescript
const samsaraStopIds = new Set(samsaraStops.map(s => s.id));
const orphanedStops = yourSystemStops.filter(
  s => !samsaraStopIds.has(s.samsaraJobId)
);
// Unschedule orphans in your system
```

## External IDs for TMS Integration
```json
{
  "externalIds": {
    "tms": "ORDER-123",
    "erp": "SHIP-456"
  }
}
```

Lookup: `GET /fleet/routes/tms:ORDER-123`

## Status Mapping
```typescript
const STATUS_MAP = {
  'scheduled': 'PENDING',
  'en route': 'ENROUTE',
  'arrived': 'ARRIVED',
  'departed': 'COMPLETED',
  'completed': 'COMPLETED',
  'skipped': 'CANCELLED'
};

// GUARD: Never revert completed status
if (currentStatus === 'COMPLETED' && newStatus !== 'COMPLETED') {
  return; // Don't update
}
```

## Webhook Signature Verification
```typescript
import crypto from 'crypto';

function verifyWebhook(payload: string, signature: string, secret: string): boolean {
  const hmac = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret);
  const digest = hmac.update(payload).digest('hex');
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(
    Buffer.from(signature),
    Buffer.from(digest)
  );
}
```

## Address Parsing
```typescript
function parseAddress(location: SamsaraLocation) {
  return {
    formatted: location.formattedAddress || '',
    latitude: location.latitude,
    longitude: location.longitude,
    name: location.name || ''
  };
}
```

## Key Endpoints

### Routes
- `POST /fleet/routes` - Create route
- `PATCH /fleet/routes/{id}` - Update route (MUST preserve stop IDs)
- `GET /fleet/routes/{id}` - Get route details
- `DELETE /fleet/routes/{id}` - Delete route

### Vehicles
- `GET /fleet/vehicles/stats/feed` - Real-time vehicle data
- `GET /fleet/vehicles` - List vehicles
- `GET /fleet/vehicles/{id}` - Vehicle details

### Locations
- `POST /fleet/locations/feed` - Real-time location feed

### Drivers
- `GET /fleet/drivers` - List drivers
- `POST /fleet/drivers` - Create driver

### Webhooks
- `POST /webhooks` - Create webhook
- `GET /webhooks` - List webhooks

## Error Handling
```typescript
async function callSamsaraAPI(endpoint: string, options: RequestInit) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(endpoint, options);
    
    if (response.status === 429) {
      const retryAfter = response.headers.get('Retry-After');
      await sleep(retryAfter ? parseInt(retryAfter) * 1000 : 1000);
      return callSamsaraAPI(endpoint, options); // Retry
    }
    
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`Samsara API error: ${response.statusText}`);
    }
    
    return await response.json();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Samsara API call failed:', error);
    throw error;
  }
}
```

## Best Practices
1. Always fetch existing route before updating to preserve stop IDs
2. Use feed endpoints for real-time data (poll every 5-10 sec)
3. Implement conservative rate limiting (5 req/sec default)
4. Use external IDs for bidirectional sync
5. Verify webhook signatures with HMAC SHA-256
6. Never revert completed stops to earlier statuses
7. Handle orphaned stops when syncing bidirectionally
8. Use exponential backoff with jitter on rate limit errors

## Common Mistakes to Avoid
❌ Updating routes without fetching existing stop IDs first
❌ Polling feeds faster than 5 seconds
❌ Ignoring rate limit headers
❌ Not verifying webhook signatures
❌ Reverting completed statuses
❌ Using snapshot endpoints for continuous tracking
❌ Hardcoding base URLs (respect region)
❌ Not handling 429 responses with backoff

---

When writing Samsara integration code, always:
1. Check which region (US/EU) the customer uses
2. Preserve stop IDs when updating routes
3. Implement proper rate limiting
4. Use external IDs for TMS linking
5. Verify webhook signatures
6. Follow the data sync pattern appropriate for the use case
